==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmɔrɡən/|[ˈmɔʁ-]|[ˈmɔɐ̯-]|[ˈmɔː-]|[-ɡən]|[-ɡŋ̍]}}
* {{IPA|de|/mɔrŋ/|/mɔrjən/}} {{q|colloquial variants}}
* {{audio|de|De-Morgen.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|morgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|morgan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*morgin|*morgan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*murginaz|*murganaz}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*merkʷ-||to blink, twinkle}}. 

Compare {{cog|nds|Morgen}}, {{cog|nl|morgen}}, {{cog|fy|moarn}}, {{cog|en|morn}}, {{m|en|morrow}}, {{cog|da|morgen}}, {{cog|sv|morgon}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m,,-:de[colloquial]}}

# [[morning]] {{gloss|part of the day from dawn to noon}}
#: {{syn|de|Vormittag}}
#: {{uxi|de|am '''Morgen'''|in the '''morning'''}}
#: {{uxi|de|am '''Morgen''' des 6. Dezember 2000|on the '''morning''' of the 6th December 2000}}
#: {{uxi|de|gestern '''Morgen''' (''also:'' gestern '''morgen''')|yesterday '''morning'''}}
#: {{uxi|de|heute '''Morgen'''|this '''morning'''}}
# {{lb|de|agriculture|dated}} [[morgen]] {{gloss|measure of land equivalent to two acres}}; {{lb|de|informal}} [[acre]] {{q|when speaking vaguely}}, a [[quarter]] of a [[hectare]] {{q|specific}}
# {{lb|de|archaic|poetic}} [[east]] {{gloss|direction of the rising sun at an equinox}}
#: {{syn|de|Morgenland}}
#: {{ux|de|gen '''Morgen''' gehen|walk in the direction where the sun rises}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The normal plural is unchanged {{m|de||Morgen}}. The dialectal plural {{m|de|Morgende}} is formed under the influence of {{m|de|Abende|t=evenings}}. It is rather common colloquially but hardly ever used in literary German.
* {{m|de||Morgen}} includes the whole time of day between dawn and noon, though the time roughly between 9 a.m. and noon is often specified as {{m|de|Vormittag}}.

